to build these suckers.

779
00:40:36,421 --> 00:40:39,420
Basically, the components are a combustion chamber,

780
00:40:39,421 --> 00:40:42,420
an igniter, and then the barrel.

781
00:40:42,421 --> 00:40:44,420
Builders sharpen one end of the pipe

782
00:40:44,421 --> 00:40:48,420
to serve as a barrel knife, shaving off excess potato

783
00:40:48,421 --> 00:40:51,420
as it's stuffed into the gun.

784
00:40:51,421 --> 00:40:54,420
This creates a tight seal.

785
00:40:54,421 --> 00:40:57,420
Next, the propellant.

786
00:40:57,421 --> 00:41:00,420
We like to use hairspray and deodorant.

787
00:41:00,421 --> 00:41:03,420
Especially deodorant on days like this.

788
00:41:03,421 --> 00:41:05,420
Once sealed in the small end of the chamber,

789
00:41:05,421 --> 00:41:09,420
a mere spark from a barbecue lighter creates an explosion.

790
00:41:09,421 --> 00:41:12,420
a mere spark from a barbecue lighter creates an explosion.

791
00:41:14,920 --> 00:41:17,420
Pressure builds rapidly behind the wedged potato

792
00:41:17,421 --> 00:41:19,800
and forces it down the barrel and out.

793
00:41:21,700 --> 00:41:22,400
Boom.

794
00:41:23,500 --> 00:41:24,780
So that's the basics.

795
00:41:25,300 --> 00:41:27,040
But where is the gunner who doesn't crave

796
00:41:27,041 --> 00:41:28,620
to customize his potato shooter,

797
00:41:29,380 --> 00:41:31,240
including a laser sight?

798
00:41:31,580 --> 00:41:34,140
There's a level on it and just a little laser pointer,

799
00:41:34,280 --> 00:41:35,720
and you get it shooting right down the barrel.

800
00:41:36,220 --> 00:41:38,280
And on evenings, you can see,

801
00:41:38,281 --> 00:41:39,980
You just point the dot on your target,

802
00:41:40,080 --> 00:41:42,520
and it's pretty accurate.

803
00:41:42,620 --> 00:41:43,820
But what if you want your potato

804
00:41:43,920 --> 00:41:45,120
to take a longer trip?

805
00:41:49,620 --> 00:41:56,040
What if you replace deodorant with rocket fuel?

806
00:41:56,140 --> 00:41:58,340
Put yourself in the shoes of a NASA scientist

807
00:41:58,440 --> 00:42:00,740
planning a manned trip to Mars.

808
00:42:00,840 --> 00:42:02,680
It's a journey that will take years.

809
00:42:02,780 --> 00:42:04,780
Among the algorithms and telemetries

810
00:42:04,880 --> 00:42:06,940
is a simple yet nagging problem.

811
00:42:06,941 --> 00:42:09,540
How do you feed your astronauts?

812
00:42:09,640 --> 00:42:13,640
On long-term space flights, it's impossible

813
00:42:13,740 --> 00:42:17,380
to pack enough freeze-dried meals

814
00:42:17,480 --> 00:42:21,880
and carry all of that weight for the long-term of the endeavor.

815
00:42:21,980 --> 00:42:29,000
So it's important to grow the food that the crew will need.

816
00:42:29,100 --> 00:42:30,200
Makes sense.

817
00:42:30,300 --> 00:42:32,040
But how would you do that?

818
00:42:32,140 --> 00:42:33,440
Where's the dirt?

819
00:42:33,540 --> 00:42:35,640
And what do you grow?

820
00:42:35,641 --> 00:42:39,840
In this chamber, we have some mini tuber potatoes

821
00:42:39,940 --> 00:42:42,680
that were planted in here about a week ago.

822
00:42:42,780 --> 00:42:45,180
And you can readily see how much growth we've got

823
00:42:45,280 --> 00:42:46,580
during that time.

824
00:42:46,680 --> 00:42:51,620
You can see the formation of the stems, the roots.

825
00:42:51,720 --> 00:42:54,860
Very nice root development in one week's time.

826
00:42:54,960 --> 00:42:57,700
In 1995, the potato was the first food

827
00:42:57,800 --> 00:43:03,560
ever grown in orbit using a technology called aeroponics.

828
00:43:03,561 --> 00:43:06,220
Unlike hydroponics, which submerges a portion of the plant

829
00:43:06,221 --> 00:43:10,160
in water, aeroponics concentrates a small mist

830
00:43:10,161 --> 00:43:14,500
of nutrients onto the plant suspended in air.

831
00:43:14,501 --> 00:43:19,700
The aeroponic spray, or mist, is delivered to the plants

832
00:43:19,701 --> 00:43:21,320
on a timed interval.

833
00:43:21,321 --> 00:43:27,020
The interval delivers a three-second spray that is just,

834
00:43:27,021 --> 00:43:29,120
just like that, and that's, and it's over.

835
00:43:29,121 --> 00:43:33,560
And that is enough to coat the plant stem and the root system.

836
00:43:33,561 --> 00:43:36,160
The plant doesn't have to fight through layers of dirt,

837
00:43:36,260 --> 00:43:38,260
enhancing rapid growth.

838
00:43:38,360 --> 00:43:40,600
The plants being suspended in air,

839
00:43:40,700 --> 00:43:43,400
they're able to grow much faster.

840
00:43:43,500 --> 00:43:46,900
You can get twice or three times the rate of growth here

841
00:43:47,000 --> 00:43:48,600
that you would in a greenhouse.

842
00:43:48,700 --> 00:43:51,420
The results are remarkable.

843
00:43:51,520 --> 00:43:55,920
Aeroponically grown potatoes require 60% less water,

844
00:43:56,020 --> 00:43:59,320
90% less fertilizers like nitrogen,

845
00:43:59,420 --> 00:44:01,220
and 100% less pesticides.

846
00:44:03,560 --> 00:44:06,100
For now, aeroponics remains focused on research

847
00:44:06,101 --> 00:44:08,900
and small commercial ventures.

848
00:44:08,901 --> 00:44:12,400
No one suggests that it will replace the traditional farm,

849
00:44:12,401 --> 00:44:14,800
at least not on our planet.

850
00:44:14,801 --> 00:44:16,600
But it does make you think.

851
00:44:16,601 --> 00:44:20,320
Colorful, nutritious, beloved.

852
00:44:20,321 --> 00:44:24,520
Maybe the humble spud isn't always just a side dish.

853
00:44:24,521 --> 00:44:26,520
Sometimes it can be a star.

